# A table's columns are shared by all of its rows (buri#177). Each picture is
# drawn twice, once as a `Role.Table` and once as a column of plain grids
# whose tracks are the widths the table's columns should come to, and both
# tests compare against the same golden. The grids recorded the goldens, so a
# table that lays out any other way fails against a picture its own layout
# had no part in.
#
# Every box holds a darker block of a fixed width, so each width is whole
# pixels and no golden depends on how text is shaped.
#
#   * **`columns-shrunk.png`**: a table in a row, so it is as wide as its
#     content. Each column is its widest block — 120, 60 and 200 — although
#     no single row holds all three, so the header and both rows line up at
#     x=120 and x=180. Laid out a row at a time, each row divided itself into
#     thirds of its own.
#   * **`columns-full.png`**: the same table across the page. The 420 pixels
#     the blocks do not need go to the columns in proportion to their widest
#     block, 120 : 60 : 200, which is how a browser's automatic table layout
#     shares out the room. The boundaries land at 252.6 and 378.9.
#   * **`columns-own-tracks.png`**: the issue's own program. A row that names
#     its own `Layout(.Grid([.Fixed(.Px(600)), .Auto]))` keeps it, so its first
#     box is 600 wide rather than half the page.
#
# Checked against Chromium: the same trees as `<table>`s under the sheet's
# reset put the column boundaries at the same x in all three.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs. Textproto,
# but not a Buri file: only repo/ below is a Buri repository.

doc: "a table's columns are sized over every row at once and share the room in proportion to their content, and a row that names its own tracks keeps them, each picture matching the grid of the widths it should come to"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/columns", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "pass.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/columns/test/__snapshots__/columns-shrunk.diff.png"  exists: false }
path { path: "lib/columns/test/__snapshots__/columns-full.diff.png"  exists: false }
path { path: "lib/columns/test/__snapshots__/columns-own-tracks.diff.png"  exists: false }
